   "summary": "A release about building by hand. A part turns about any of its own axes by rings and arrows on it, Connect puts a point on one part onto a point on another at any angle, a number typed while you move a part moves it exactly that far, and copies go down in a row or a ring at once. Split swaps a part for smaller real parts and Merge does the reverse, a set's own bin follows its booklet, and the Library opens on real sets drawn in 3D. Every tool has a key, and Studio's, Mecabricks' or LDCad's keys come as presets, so your hands already know it. Two people building together see each other's pointer and pin comments to parts, a model's build plays as a video, and Claude, or another AI on your own key, can design for you.",
